import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---
<DocsLayout title="API Reference | Agent-Gantry">
  <h1>API reference</h1>
  <h2>Primary imports</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from agent_gantry import (
    AgentGantry, create_default_gantry, with_semantic_tools,
    set_default_gantry, ToolCall, ToolResult, ToolDefinition,
    GantryContextProvider, enable_console_logging,
)`} />
  <h2>AgentGantry</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>register(...)</code>: register a callable as a tool, with tags, capabilities, metadata, and schema inference.</li>
    <li><code>sync()</code>: synchronize tool definitions to the configured vector store.</li>
    <li><code>retrieve(...)</code> / <code>retrieve_tools(...)</code>: retrieve relevant tools for a query and return internal or provider-specific schemas.</li>
    <li><code>execute(ToolCall)</code>: execute a selected call through the execution engine.</li>
    <li><code>close()</code>: release vector store, telemetry, and protocol resources.</li>
    <li><code>add_mcp_server(MCPServerConfig(command=[...] | url="https://..."))</code>: discover tools from a local (stdio) or remote (Streamable HTTP / SSE) MCP server; <code>register_mcp_server(...)</code> registers server metadata for semantic server selection.</li>
    <li><code>serve_mcp(transport="stdio" | "http" | "sse", mode="dynamic" | "static" | "hybrid", expose=[...])</code>: expose the registry as an MCP server.</li>
    <li><code>add_skills_from_directory(path)</code> / <code>retrieve_skills_as_prompt(query)</code>: load Agent Skills (<code>SKILL.md</code>) and inject only the relevant ones per prompt.</li>
    <li><code>sync(prune=True)</code>: also remove stored tools that are no longer registered.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Decorator path</h2>
  <p><code>with_semantic_tools</code> wraps existing async generation functions and injects a <code>tools</code> argument based on the prompt parameter.</p>
  <h2>CLI</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`agent-gantry list --module my_app.tools
agent-gantry search "refund an order" --module my_app.tools --limit 3
agent-gantry sync --dry-run --prune --module my_app.tools
agent-gantry serve-mcp --module my_app.tools --transport http --mode hybrid --expose get_weather
agent-gantry install-skill --claude
agent-gantry install-skill --target ./skills`} />
  <p>Every inspection command accepts <code>--module pkg.tools[:attr]</code> and then operates on that module's own <code>AgentGantry</code> instance (its embedder, its vector store). Without it a small demo registry is used.</p>
</DocsLayout>
